Tool call input: {'knowledge_bases': ['pubmed_papers'], 'search_rounds_budget': 3, 'search_target': 'Search PubMed for direct studies in HIV/HCV-coinfected patients evaluating statin use (HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors) and incident cirrhosis or progression to cirrhosis. Return citations/PMIDs and quantitative adjusted effect estimates; report if no direct studies are identified and distinguish general HCV cohorts.'}

The direct study supports a qualified “yes”: in a large observational HIV/HCV veteran cohort, greater statin exposure was associated with lower cirrhosis risk among those with ALT ≤40 IU/L, but the association was subgroup-specific and does not prove causation. I’ll check the evidence graph for existing matching entities before adding this result. Plan: 1 [✓] Literature search completed; direct study identified (PMID 27753678). 2 [✓] Abstract and comparator evidence reviewed; key design, result, and limitations assessed. 3 [ ] Check graph for duplicates, then record concise evidence and provenance; finalize.

